{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjCanonicalKnotIdSdp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjCanonicalKnotIdSdp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness"],"declarations":50,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_subsingleton_under_strict_complementarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_subsingleton_under_strict_complementarity","kind":"theorem","line":700,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L700-L707","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_existence_with_witness_rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_existence_with_witness_rho","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L654-L667","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_canonical_uniqueness_pending_hoefsmit_h5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_canonical_uniqueness_pending_hoefsmit_h5","kind":"def","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L576-L608","doc":"**Tritium pipeline deferred (PR #608 deliverable for ³H).**\n\nThe R5-full prototype does not yet support `tritium` because the\nHoefsmit seminormal at H_5 is currently implemented only in\nRust (`tools/hecke-engine`).  Once a Python port lands, the\nsame `helium3_canonical_uniqueness_via_strict_complementarity`\nstructural argument applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuterium_canonical_uniqueness_pending_multiterm_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuterium_canonical_uniqueness_pending_multiterm_cost","kind":"def","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L536-L574","doc":"**Multi-term cost wiring (PR #608 followup #1).**\n\nStatus of this theorem for the other nuclei depends on extending\n`r5_full_canonical_knot_solver.cost_for_candidate` from the\nsingle-term flagship `B = m_e ρ |tr_M(T_w)|` to the multi-term\nformula T2–T6 of `thm:knot-mass-formula-unified`.  Without the\nmulti-term cost, the prototype's L=8 winner for deuteron is\n`σ_2 σ_1^6 σ_2^{-1}` (PSD-feasible at α_gap = 0) rather than\nthe historical `6_2`.  Wiring the multi-term cost would change\nthe search's score function and (per the conjecture) recover\n`6_2` as the unique minimizer.  This is sub-deliverable 3 of\nIssue #604 specialised to `deuterium`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_canonical_uniqueness_via_strict_complementarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_canonical_uniqueness_via_strict_complementarity","kind":"def","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L463-L534","doc":"**Categorical uniqueness theorem (closure path for GAP-A-1).**\n\nGiven the R5-full numerical witness for nucleus `n` AND a\ncategorical strict-complementarity certificate, the SDP\nminimizer `T_w*` recorded in\n`r5-full-canonical-knot-solver.witness.json` is the unique\noptimal Hecke element in the feasible region.  This is the\nstructural upgrade of the `canonical` skeleton instance\nabove: that instance carries the historical knot id with\n`rho := 1`, while this theorem proves the SDP-uniqueness\nstatement upon receipt of the strict-complementarity\ncertificate.\n\nStatus (2026-05-09):\n* `helium3` — R5-full witness has α_gap = 0 (PSD-feasible) for\n  L_6a4 = (σ_1 σ_2^{-1})^3; strict-complementarity is the\n  remaining categorical hypothesis.  ³He's witness shows all\n  three Wedderburn-block min_eigs > 0 (trivial: 1.87, standard:\n  0.53, sign: 0.53), so the active set is **empty** — the\n  optimum is in the interior of the feasible region.  Strict\n  complementarity is vacuously satisfied; uniqueness reduces\n  to strict convexity of the Frobenius cost on the interior.\n* `deuterium` — R5-full witness's winner at L_max=8 is\n  σ_2 σ_1^6 σ_2^{-1}, **not** the historical 6_2.  The\n  single-term cost function does not select 6_2 at first\n  principle; multi-term wiring (T2–T6 of\n  thm:knot-mass-formula-unified) is the next-priority step\n  per PR #608's followup list.\n* `tritium` — R5-full pipeline deferred (Hoefsmit at H_5\n  pending).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.inactive_dual_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.inactive_dual_zero","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L461-L461","doc":"The inactive-set dual variables are exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.active_dual_pos_or_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.active_dual_pos_or_empty","kind":"theorem","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L459-L459","doc":"The active-set dual variables are positive (or vacuous if the\nactive set is empty per `min_block_eig > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.max_inactive_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.max_inactive_dual","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L456-L456","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.min_dual_y_on_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.min_dual_y_on_active","kind":"def","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L455-L455","doc":"Active set is empty when `min_block_eig > 0`; in that case the\nstrict-complementarity inequalities below hold vacuously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.min_block_eig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.min_block_eig","kind":"def","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L452-L452","doc":"Concrete real-valued field: minimum eigenvalue across all\nWedderburn blocks in the witness's `per_block_summary`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L448-L448","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StrictComplementarity","kind":"structure","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L419-L461","doc":"**StrictComplementarity** — categorical hypothesis upgrading\nthe numerical R5-full witness to uniqueness.\n\nA primal–dual pair `(T_w*, y*)` for the R5-full SDP satisfies\n*strict complementarity* iff for each Frobenius/Wedderburn\nconstraint `i`:\n* either `y*_i > 0` (the constraint is binding) and the slack\n  at `T_w*` is exactly zero,\n* or `y*_i = 0` (the constraint is inactive) and the slack is\n  strictly positive.\n\nStrict complementarity in convex programming implies the\nprimal optimum is unique (Boyd–Vandenberghe §5.5).  The\nR5-full witness records the primal–dual data; whether the\nstructural inequalities hold is a categorical question about\nthe geometry of the feasible set.\n\nConcrete fields (per Gemini review):\n* `min_block_eig` — minimum Wedderburn-block min-eigenvalue\n  across the witness's `per_block_summary`.  Active set is\n  empty iff this is positive.\n* `min_dual_y_on_active` — minimum dual variable value on the\n  active set (binding constraints).  Strict complementarity\n  requires this to be strictly positive whenever the active\n  set is non-empty.\n* `max_inactive_dual` — maximum dual variable value on the\n  inactive set (slack constraints).  Strict complementarity\n  requires this to be exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.rho_star_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.rho_star_pos","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L417-L417","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.rho_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.rho_star","kind":"def","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L416-L416","doc":"The chosen multiplicity ρ at the search winner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.duality_gap_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.duality_gap_le","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L414-L414","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.dual_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.dual_obj","kind":"def","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L413-L413","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.primal_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.primal_obj","kind":"def","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L412-L412","doc":"Witness records strong duality at the recorded primal/dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.alpha_gap_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.alpha_gap_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L410-L410","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.alpha_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.alpha_gap","kind":"def","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L409-L409","doc":"α-gap from the SDP search (PSD-feasible iff `alpha_gap = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L407-L407","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.R5FullWitness","kind":"class","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L391-L417","doc":"**R5FullWitness** — the numerical certificate produced by\nPR #608's `r5_full_canonical_knot_solver.py`.\n\nRecords the LP/SDP primal–dual data per AGENTS.md \"LP / SDP\nduals — first-class infra\" and the per-Wedderburn-block\nPSD-feasibility check.  An instance asserts that for nucleus\n`n`, the prototype produced a feasible candidate `T_w` in the\nR5-full search at depth `L_max`, with the recorded primal\nobjective, dual variables, and Wedderburn-block min-eigenvalues\ndocumented in the witness JSON\n`r5-full-canonical-knot-solver.witness.json`.\n\nThis is a *numerical* certificate; the categorical uniqueness\ntheorem below upgrades it to a structural claim by adding a\nstrict-complementarity hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingKWord_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingKWord_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L384-L389","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_binding_K_is_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_binding_K_is_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L373-L374","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_extraction_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_extraction_pos","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L360-L361","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_helium3","kind":"instance","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L337-L345","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_tritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_tritium","kind":"instance","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L322-L330","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_deuterium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instCanonicalKnotIdSDP_deuterium","kind":"instance","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L302-L315","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.structurallyValidBinding_strand_count_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.structurallyValidBinding_strand_count_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L235-L249","doc":"Any `structurallyValidBinding w n_0` requires `4 ≤ n_0`: the\nword is non-empty (so contains some generator `g`), and\n`inInterNucleonRange` requires `3 ≤ |g| < n_0`, hence\n`n_0 ≥ 4`.  Useful downstream as a soundness check on any\nproposed nucleus's `n.n₀ = 3·n.A`: the lemma forces `A ≥ 2`\n(since `n_0 = 3·A ≥ 4 ⟹ A ≥ 2`), correctly excluding the\nsingle-nucleon case from any binding-K instantiation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKLengthBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKLengthBounded","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L226-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKEvenPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKEvenPower","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L225-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKStructurallyValid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKStructurallyValid","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L224-L224","doc":"── Decidable structural sub-Props (Lean-checkable). ─────────\nThese are the concrete, kernel-verifiable predicates over\n`bindingKWord` that the per-nucleus instances actually\ndischarge.  The semantic Props above are placeholders; the\nstructural Props below are the LEAN-VERIFIED content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.rho_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.rho_pos","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L184-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.rho","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L183-L183","doc":"The SDP minimizer is achieved at this multiplicity ρ ≥ 1.\nPer conj:rho-prefactor-structural, this comes from the\ndominant Wedderburn summand of `bindingK n` at H_{n.n₀}(q₀). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingKWord","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L179-L179","doc":"An explicit braid word for `bindingK n` in B_{n.n₀}.  See\n`binding-k-enumerator.witness.json` for the empirical winners. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingLinkName","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.bindingLinkName","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L176-L176","doc":"Name of the binding-link operator K ∈ H_{n.n₀}(q₀)\n(e.g. \"L_H Hopf\" for ²H, \"L6a4\" for ³He). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.canonicalKnotId","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.canonicalKnotId","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L173-L173","doc":"Name of the canonical knot / link (e.g. \"6_2\", \"8_11\", \"L6a4\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP.mk","kind":"ctor","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDP","kind":"class","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L171-L226","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:canonical-knot-id-sdp","label":"conj:canonical-knot-id-sdp","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.evenPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.evenPower","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L159-L166","doc":"An *even-power* binding word — every generator's signed power\nsums to an even number — is the simplest sufficient condition\nfor the σ_k blocks to give all-positive eigenvalues\n(σ_k^{2m} has eigenvalues q^{2m}, q^{-2m} > 0).  This is a\nnecessary-but-not-sufficient PSD-feasibility proxy in absence\nof full Hecke-block evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.structurallyValidBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.structurallyValidBinding","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L153-L157","doc":"A binding word is *structurally valid* iff it is non-empty,\nevery generator is non-zero, and every generator is in the\ninter-nucleon range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.inInterNucleonRange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.inInterNucleonRange","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L139-L151","doc":"Every generator in `w` is in the inter-nucleon range\n`[3, n_0 - 1]` (in absolute value).  These are the generators\nthat cross between distinct nucleon-strand triples; intra-nucleon\ngenerators (σ_1, σ_2 within nucleon 1; σ_4, σ_5 within nucleon 2;\netc.) are σ_{3k+1}, σ_{3k+2} for k = 0, 1, ..., A-1.  The\ninter-nucleon generators are σ_{3k} for k = 1, ..., A-1.\n\nFor a strict \"minimal-binding-only\" predicate, restrict to the\nstrict inter-nucleon set {σ_{3k}}; for the \"extended\" search\n(allowing intra-nucleon-2/3 twists in the binding) we accept\nany |g| in [3, n_0 - 1]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.allNonZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord.allNonZero","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L135-L137","doc":"Every generator index in `w` is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraidWord","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L123-L125","doc":"An explicit braid word in B_{n.n₀} encoded as a list of nonzero\ngenerator indices (positive ⇒ σ_i, negative ⇒ σ_i^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.numConstituents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.numConstituents","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The number of constituents (nucleons) of a `LightNucleus`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.n₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.n₀","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L71-L73","doc":"The atomic strand count `n₀ = 3 · A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.A","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L65-L69","doc":"The atomic mass number `A` of a `LightNucleus`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.helium3","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.tritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.tritium","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.deuterium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus.deuterium","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus","kind":"inductive","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean#L58-L63","doc":"Enumeration of the three light nuclei whose canonical knot\nidentification this conjecture addresses. ","signatureChunk":0}]}